{
  "_comment": [
    "ECS task definition for rithm-worker. Replace <ACCOUNT>, <SECRET_RDS_ARN>,",
    "<JOBS_QUEUE_URL>, <ASSETS_BUCKET>, <ACESTEP_API_BASE> and the image tag",
    "before registering.",
    "",
    "*** THIS SHAPE CHANGED AFTER THE PoC. READ THIS BEFORE REGISTERING. ***",
    "",
    "ACE-Step v1.5 turned out to be an HTTP SERVER (git checkout + uv sync),",
    "not a Python library. The worker therefore holds no model: it POSTs to",
    "/release_task, polls /query_result and downloads the audio. Everything",
    "GPU-shaped has moved OFF this container:",
    "",
    "  resourceRequirements GPU=1   REMOVED — this container never touches CUDA",
    "  linuxParameters.sharedMemorySize  REMOVED — no torch DataLoader here",
    "  ACESTEP_WEIGHTS_DIR / ACESTEP_REPO_ID  REMOVED — nothing is baked in",
    "  cpu/memory                   dropped from 7168/28672 to 1024/2048. The",
    "      worker downloads audio, runs ffmpeg loudnorm + mp3 encode, and",
    "      uploads. That is the whole workload.",
    "",
    "The image is now 914 MB on disk / 230 MB compressed, down from 22.7 GB /",
    "8.19 GB — the single biggest change to cold start. `--target production`",
    "and `--target stub` now produce a BYTE-IDENTICAL image; only",
    "RITHM_STUB_INFERENCE tells them apart. Measure the real pull at J4 before",
    "setting the API's",
    "ESTIMATED_COLD_START_SECONDS — the old 4-6 minute estimate was sized for",
    "pulling a CUDA image with weights in it and is now far too pessimistic.",
    "",
    "WHERE THE GPU WENT — a Track A decision this file cannot make for you:",
    "",
    "  (a) SIDECAR: add a second container to THIS task definition running the",
    "      ACE-Step image, give THAT container resourceRequirements GPU=1 and",
    "      the memory, and set ACESTEP_API_BASE=http://localhost:8001. Keeps",
    "      the EC2 + capacity-provider + scale-from-zero design intact, and the",
    "      model dies with the worker so nothing idles at GPU prices.",
    "  (b) STANDALONE: run ACE-Step on its own always-on GPU box (what the PoC",
    "      did) and point ACESTEP_API_BASE at its DNS. The worker then has no",
    "      GPU dependency at all and could move to FARGATE, deleting the ASG,",
    "      the capacity provider and the GPU AMI from the design. Cheaper to",
    "      operate, but you pay for the GPU box whether or not anyone",
    "      generates, and the model becomes a single point of failure shared",
    "      across tasks.",
    "",
    "Whichever you pick, the WORKER CODE IS IDENTICAL — only ACESTEP_API_BASE",
    "differs. Do not let that make the choice feel reversible on the AWS side:",
    "(a) and (b) are different infrastructure.",
    "",
    "Note also: ffmpeg is NOT in Amazon Linux 2023's base repositories. It is",
    "baked into this image, so this container is fine — but any host running",
    "the ACE-Step server that also post-processes audio needs it installed",
    "explicitly.",
    "",
    "OTHER SETTINGS THAT ARE NOT ARBITRARY:",
    "",
    "  RITHM_STUB_INFERENCE   must be ABSENT here. Rev 1 (Gate D) sets it to",
    "      '1' and omits ACESTEP_API_BASE. A leftover '1' means every check",
    "      goes green while producing a canned 5-second WAV.",
    "  WORKER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS 600   rev 1 uses '0' so the box holds still",
    "      while you SSM into it.",
    "  stopTimeout 120        paired with ECS_CONTAINER_STOP_TIMEOUT=5m in the",
    "      launch template's user-data. Without the instance-level value the",
    "      agent SIGKILLs at 30s regardless of what is set here.",
    "  SQS_VISIBILITY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS 900   the queue default is 300. Measured",
    "      generation is far quicker than that (LM 6-14s + DiT ~7s at 180s),",
    "      but 900 costs nothing and covers a slow model server plus a ~60 MB",
    "      upload. When the timeout is exceeded SQS redelivers a job that is",
    "      still running: harmless (the claim guard drops it) but it burns one",
    "      of three receives and creeps the job toward the DLQ.",
    "  ACESTEP_SEND_SEED      absent, i.e. off. The PoC could not confirm that",
    "      /release_task accepts a seed. Until someone does, the server picks",
    "      its own and variations differ by chance rather than by construction.",
    "",
    "SNS_COMPLETIONS_TOPIC_ARN is deliberately ABSENT. The worker publishes to",
    "the callback_topic_arn carried in each job envelope, never a configured",
    "one — that is what the task role scopes and what keeps the image",
    "environment-agnostic."
  ],
  "family": "rithm-worker",
  "networkMode": "awsvpc",
  "requiresCompatibilities": ["EC2"],
  "executionRoleArn": "arn:aws:iam::<ACCOUNT>:role/ecsTaskExecutionRole",
  "taskRoleArn": "arn:aws:iam::<ACCOUNT>:role/rithm-worker-task-role",
  "containerDefinitions": [
    {
      "name": "worker",
      "image": "<ACCOUNT>.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/rithm/worker:<REAL_SHA>",
      "essential": true,
      "cpu": 1024,
      "memory": 2048,
      "stopTimeout": 120,
      "environment": [
        { "name": "AWS_REGION", "value": "us-east-1" },
        { "name": "SQS_JOBS_QUEUE_URL", "value": "<JOBS_QUEUE_URL>" },
        { "name": "ASSETS_BUCKET", "value": "<ASSETS_BUCKET>" },
        { "name": "LOG_LEVEL", "value": "INFO" },
        { "name": "WORKER_IDLE_EXIT_SECONDS", "value": "600" },
        { "name": "SQS_VISIBILITY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "value": "900" },
        { "name": "MAX_LENGTH_SECONDS", "value": "180" },
        { "name": "ACESTEP_API_BASE", "value": "<ACESTEP_API_BASE>" },
        { "name": "ACESTEP_TASK_TYPE", "value": "text2music" },
        { "name": "ACESTEP_DIT_MODEL", "value": "acestep-v15-turbo" }
      ],
      "secrets": [
        {
          "name": "DB_GENERATION_DSN_SYNC",
          "valueFrom": "<SECRET_RDS_ARN>:generation_dsn_sync::"
        }
      ],
      "logConfiguration": {
        "logDriver": "awslogs",
        "options": {
          "awslogs-group": "/ecs/rithm-worker",
          "awslogs-region": "us-east-1",
          "awslogs-stream-prefix": "worker",
          "awslogs-create-group": "true"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
